  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected native inputs authenticate the named methods and ordinary signatures, stored fields and enum identities, complete reviewed body windows, linked direct calls and branches, and arithmetic/return witnesses. These byte checks retain the reviewed interpretation; they do not discover new formulas.",
    "direct": "On the normally returning unpatched DamageAction._ProcessDamage path, the action's damageUnits list is indexed and saved. That same DamageUnit's nonnull poiseCalculation gates a separate PoisePackData path. After PoisePackData construction and its before-calculation ApplyPoiseModifier call, the stored poiseCalculation pointer is passed to the calculation-object dispatch helper. Its returned CalcResult.value is copied into the PoisePackData.calcResult.value slot. This route is independent of the DamageUnit.simpleCalculation attack selector.",
    "conditional": "The reviewed normal native patch-table guards must select the default path, all named providers must return normally, and any post-evaluation guard must allow the result copy. The current indirect patch path bypasses these calculations; its provider internals and live selection are not claimed.",
    "unresolved": "The virtual subtype target selected by the helper, exact live patch state, executed action, blackboard provider values, downstream Poise modifiers and factors, immunity handling, final applied or displayed Poise amount, and any final damage result remain unproved."
  },
